---
import MainLayout from '../layouts/MainLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import DrainSymptoms from '../components/DrainSymptoms.astro';
import WhereDrainsGoWrong from '../components/WhereDrainsGoWrong.astro';
import ServicesGrid from '../components/ServicesGrid.astro';
import ContactCTA from '../components/ContactCTA.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import GoogleBusinessInfo from '../components/GoogleBusinessInfo.astro';
import ServiceAreaCityLinks from '../components/ServiceAreaCityLinks.astro';
---

<MainLayout
  title="A-1 Drain Cleaning | Drain Cleaning & Sewer Service in Mason City, Iowa"
  description="A-1 Drain Cleaning cleans and unclogs floor drains, main drains and sewer lines in Mason City and North Iowa. Call 641-530-2728 for drain backups."
  path="/"
>
  <Header />
  <main id="main">
    <Hero />
    <DrainSymptoms />
    <WhereDrainsGoWrong />

    <ServicesGrid />

    <section class="bg-slate-100 py-16 sm:py-20">
      <div class="container grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[.8fr_1.2fr] lg:items-start">
        <div>
          <p class="text-sm font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#b4232b]">Equipment &amp; methods</p>
          <h2 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-950 sm:text-5xl">The right tool depends on the line.</h2>
          <p class="mt-4 max-w-xl leading-7 text-slate-700">A-1 uses the equipment that fits the blockage, access, and condition of the pipe. A cable machine may be right for one line; roots, heavy buildup, or a recurring problem may call for another method.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <article class="border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5"><h3 class="font-black">Drain machines</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">Different cable sizes and tree root removal equipment help remove drain and sewer blockages when suited to the line and the problem.</p></article>
          <article class="border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5"><h3 class="font-black">Sewer cameras</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">A camera can show what is inside a sewer line when a recurring problem needs more investigation.</p></article>
          <article class="border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5"><h3 class="font-black">Line locating</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">Locating equipment can help identify where an underground sewer or drain line runs.</p></article>
          <article class="border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5"><h3 class="font-black">Hydro-jetting</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">Pressurized water can clean buildup when jetting is appropriate for the pipe and blockage.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <ServiceAreaCityLinks />

    <section class="bg-white py-16 sm:py-20" aria-labelledby="about-a1-heading">
      <div class="container grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1fr] lg:items-start">
        <article>
          <p class="text-sm font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#b4232b]">Local drain and sewer work</p>
          <h2 id="about-a1-heading" class="mt-2 text-4xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-950 sm:text-5xl">A-1 Drain Cleaning in Mason City, Iowa</h2>
          <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-8 text-slate-700">Josh Theilen owns A-1 Drain Cleaning, based in Mason City and serving homes and businesses across North Iowa. The work centers on clearing clogged drains, cleaning main lines, removing roots from sewer lines, and investigating recurring backups.</p>
          <a href="/about/" class="mt-6 inline-flex min-h-11 items-center font-black text-[#b4232b] underline decoration-2 underline-offset-4">More about A-1 Drain Cleaning →</a>
        </article>
        <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <article class="border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-6">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-950">Homeowners</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-700">Help with basement floor drain backups, stopped sinks, clogged toilets, laundry drain overflows, and sewer lines that keep plugging up.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-6">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-950">Businesses</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-700">Drain and sewer cleaning for business properties in the North Iowa service area. Describe the affected fixtures and whether more than one drain is backing up when you call.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-slate-100 py-16 sm:py-20" aria-labelledby="homepage-faq-heading">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="text-sm font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#b4232b]">Straight answers from A-1</p>
        <h2 id="homepage-faq-heading" class="mt-2 max-w-4xl text-4xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-950 sm:text-5xl">Drain cleaning and sewer backup questions</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-slate-700">The details that matter most are where the water appears, what was running when it happened, and whether other fixtures are affected. These answers can help you describe the problem when you call A-1 Drain Cleaning.</p>

        <div class="mt-8 space-y-3">
          <details class="border border-slate-300 bg-white p-5 sm:p-6"><summary class="cursor-pointer text-lg font-black text-slate-950">Sewage is coming up through my basement floor drain. What should I do first?</summary><div class="mt-3 max-w-4xl space-y-3 leading-7 text-slate-700"><p>Stop using toilets, sinks, showers, and the washing machine as much as you can. More water going into a blocked drain system can mean more wastewater coming back into the house. Keep children and pets away from the affected area and avoid contact with the wastewater.</p><p>Call A-1 Drain Cleaning at <a href="tel:+16415302728" class="font-bold text-[#b4232b] underline underline-offset-2">641-530-2728</a>. Tell us whether the backup started after flushing, showering, or running laundry, and whether other drains are acting up too. The floor drain may be where the water escapes even if the blockage is farther down the line.</p></div></details>
          <details class="border border-slate-300 bg-white p-5 sm:p-6"><summary class="cursor-pointer text-lg font-black text-slate-950">Why does my washing machine make water come out of the floor drain or standpipe?</summary><p class="mt-3 max-w-4xl leading-7 text-slate-700">A washer pumps out a large amount of water in a short time. If the laundry drain or a shared line cannot carry that water away, it can spill from the standpipe or push water up through a nearby floor drain. Stop running the washer until the drain is checked. If other fixtures are slow or backing up, mention that when you call because it can point to a restriction farther down the system.</p></details>
          <details class="border border-slate-300 bg-white p-5 sm:p-6"><summary class="cursor-pointer text-lg font-black text-slate-950">My house has no basement. Where does a main sewer backup show up?</summary><p class="mt-3 max-w-4xl leading-7 text-slate-700">In a slab house or a home without a basement, wastewater from a blocked main drain or sewer line may back up into a bathtub or shower. You may not see a basement floor drain overflow, but the cause can still be farther down the home's drain system. Stop using water as much as possible and tell A-1 which fixtures filled or backed up first.</p></details>
          <details class="border border-slate-300 bg-white p-5 sm:p-6"><summary class="cursor-pointer text-lg font-black text-slate-950">How can I tell if I need a local drain cleaning or main drain cleaning?</summary><p class="mt-3 max-w-4xl leading-7 text-slate-700">A single slow kitchen sink, bathroom sink, or tub may have a restriction in its own drain. When several fixtures are affected together, a toilet flush causes another drain to rise, or wastewater comes up through the lowest drain, the problem may be in a shared branch or main line. These are clues, not a diagnosis; describe the pattern rather than guessing where the blockage is.</p></details>
          <details class="border border-slate-300 bg-white p-5 sm:p-6"><summary class="cursor-pointer text-lg font-black text-slate-950">Why does the sewer line keep clogging after cleaning?</summary><p class="mt-3 max-w-4xl leading-7 text-slate-700">A recurring blockage can mean the original restriction was not fully removed, or something in the pipe keeps catching waste. Tree roots can enter through joints or damaged areas, and buildup or pipe damage can also contribute. Cleaning the line may restore flow, but if the same problem returns, further inspection—such as a sewer camera when suitable—can help identify what is happening instead of repeatedly treating the symptom.</p></details>
          <details class="border border-slate-300 bg-white p-5 sm:p-6"><summary class="cursor-pointer text-lg font-black text-slate-950">What should I tell the drain cleaner when I call?</summary><p class="mt-3 max-w-4xl leading-7 text-slate-700">Tell us which fixture is affected, whether the water is slow or completely stopped, whether dirty water is coming back, and what was running when the problem started. Also mention whether more than one drain is affected and whether this has happened before. You do not need to know the technical name of the problem—those details help narrow down where to start.</p></details>
          <details class="border border-slate-300 bg-white p-5 sm:p-6"><summary class="cursor-pointer text-lg font-black text-slate-950">Does A-1 Drain Cleaning handle emergency drain and sewer backups?</summary><p class="mt-3 max-w-4xl leading-7 text-slate-700">A-1 Drain Cleaning offers 24/7 service for drain and sewer problems in Mason City and surrounding North Iowa communities. Call <a href="tel:+16415302728" class="font-bold text-[#b4232b] underline underline-offset-2">641-530-2728</a> and explain what is backing up so we can discuss the problem and service needed.</p></details>
          <details class="border border-slate-300 bg-white p-5 sm:p-6"><summary class="cursor-pointer text-lg font-black text-slate-950">Which North Iowa towns does A-1 Drain Cleaning serve?</summary><p class="mt-3 max-w-4xl leading-7 text-slate-700">A-1 Drain Cleaning is based in Mason City and serves surrounding North Iowa communities. The <a href="/service-area/" class="font-bold text-[#b4232b] underline underline-offset-2">service-area page</a> lists towns in the current service area. If you are unsure about your address, call 641-530-2728 and ask.</p></details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <ContactCTA showForm />
    <GoogleBusinessInfo />
  </main>
  <Footer />
</MainLayout>
